  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Added one-call immutable fused field-analysis resource with exact input binding, bounded discriminant decomposition, partial word-prime Round-2 HNF evidence, arbitrary-size/lazy residual preservation, generated FFI ownership, and an ordinary-Python corruption-resistant checker. The checker deliberately reports every native result as an uncertified candidate until a separate local fixed-point proof is supplied. Six-case differential timings and normal/sanitized lifecycle tests are included.",
    "risks": [
      "The resource is not wired into the public maximal-order engine and must not be promoted to certified completion without independent local fixed-point evidence.",
      "Warm generated-host plus independent-check timings remain above 2 ms (about 3.2-35.8 ms across the six cases); one fused crossing does not remove Round-2-heavy tails.",
      "Linux x64 normal and ASan/UBSan witnesses pass; Linux arm64 and native Windows x64 reruns remain for the platform lane."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Run the focused lifecycle witness on Linux arm64 and native Windows x64.",
      "Design the independent fixed-point witness required to promote a complete candidate to a globally certified order.",
      "Only after that proof and public-path measurements, adopt the resource lazily in maximal_order_engine.py."
    ]
  }
